# Round mimoref: ik's CPU node dumps of the MiMo-V2.6-Flash MOPD MXFP4 split set (two shards, shard 1
# the 5,948,608 B header and shard 2 the 167,363,516,512 B of tensors: 167.4 GB in all), each one
# `just dump-ref-mimo2 [VARIANT]` under this card: the batch set, then step4, step4-every-node, d1k
# and d4096, one lease each. dump_ref loads without --defer-experts, so ik's loader populates the
# shards in turn (one stream), then computes on 32 threads, then writes the nodes to /root/bloomery-data.
# The three phases run one after the other: the wall is their sum. The one term the batch dump fixes:
# this file's cold-read rate through the loader's populate, read from the witness block's read-sectors
# and wall; the step dumps then read nothing from the device unless a run between two dumps evicted
# the file.
# Minutes per dump [derived], scaled from glmref's measured GLM dumps (199.7 GB: batch cold 133 s at
# ~1.5-1.7 GB/s, step4-every-node warm 17 s, d1k warm 29 s; commit 0b5d1c9):
#   populate  cold: 167.4 GB at 1.5-1.7 GB/s (GLM's measured rates): 98-112 s; at the single-stream
#             priors 1.07-1.33 GB/s 126-156 s. Warm: the page cache mapped again, >= 7 GB/s: <= 24 s
#   fixed     lease, witnesses, ~470 tensors' metadata over two shards, context: 3-15 s
#   compute   2 FLOP an active parameter a token at the design's 15.45 B active (SWA attn 3.68 +
#             full attn 0.80 + dense FFN 0.20 + top-8 MoE 9.46 + embed/head 1.25 + router/norms/sinks
#             0.05; scripts/derive.py, specs/leader/mimo26) = 30.9 GFLOP a token, attention over the
#             context added below, at 1.25 TFLOP/s (qwen35moe's measured 1,024-token prefill) to
#             3 TFLOP/s (GLM's d1k): batch and step4 5 tokens ~0.15 TFLOP < 1 s; d1k 1,025 tokens
#             31.7 + attention 0.6 = 32.3 TFLOP 11-26 s; d4096 4,097 tokens 126.6 + attention 7.0
#             (9 full layers x 4,097^2 x 64 x (192+128) x 2 FLOP + 39 SWA layers over the 128 window)
#             = 133.6 TFLOP 45-107 s
#   dump      2.5-4.5 GB a set (qwen35moe's 1.5-1.6 GB at 40 layers, hidden 2048; GLM's 3.3-3.8 GB
#             at 46 layers, hidden 4096, a 4-wide residual; this model 48 layers, hidden 4096, one
#             residual) at the 0.5 GB/s the qwen3moe and qwen35moe step dumps wrote: 5-9 s
#   batch cold 1.8-2.6 min; step4, step4-every-node warm 0.2-0.9 min; d1k warm 0.3-1.3 min; d4096
#   warm 0.9-2.6 min; 3.5-8.5 min in all. A step dump that reads the file from the device again (a
#   peer's run between two dumps evicted it) costs the populate term again (98-156 s); all five cold
#   is at most 12 min. A dump needs the ik tree past the fused-attn_qkv load (upstream #2556) — see
#   the profile's IK note; the walls above assume only that the loader works.
kind: exclusive
reason: dump_ref runs ik on 32 CPU threads and populates the whole 167.4 GB split set into the page
  cache, evicting that much of what else is cached (the V4.1 host set or the GLM set among it);
  beside a timed run or a gate batch it would take their cores, their memory bandwidth and their
  cache, so it holds the lease; why now: the mimo2 oracle every MiMo kernel and body round is judged
  against (round mimoref)
minutes: 0.2..2.6
